{"assignees":[{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzQ5NjM5","login":"abhishek818","name":"Abhishek Kumar Gupta","databaseId":29749639}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMzYzMA==","is_bot":false,"login":"rparcus","name":"Robert Parcus"},"body":"## Overview\n\nImplement integration with Perplexity AI for advanced language model capabilities and specialized knowledge tasks.\n\n## Core Features\n- Perplexity AI API integration\n- Specialized model access\n- Knowledge-intensive tasks\n- Response streaming\n- Cost optimization\n\n## Technical Details\n- Implement Perplexity client\n- Add streaming support\n- Set up model selection\n- Implement cost tracking\n- Add error handling\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Implement Perplexity API client\n- [ ] Add streaming response support\n- [ ] Create model selection interface\n- [ ] Implement error handling\n- [ ] Add cost tracking\n- [ ] Include documentation\n- [ ] Add integration tests\n\n## Budget: $300","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc6gQ_h_","author":{"login":"abhishek818"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@rparcus I can take this up?","createdAt":"2025-02-27T18:43:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-2688809087","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc6gWTeD","author":{"login":"rparcus"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Please go ahead!\n\nAssigned to @abhishek818 ","createdAt":"2025-02-28T09:48:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-2690201475","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc7tACnb","author":{"login":"KimberleyOCaseyfv"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Claim: Perplexity AI Integration - Technical Proposal\n\nHi @Spectral-Finance team,\n\nI'd like to work on this Perplexity AI integration. Based on my experience with LLM integrations and the Lux framework, here's my comprehensive proposal:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Technical Solution\n\n**Architecture** (following Lux prism/beam patterns):\n```\npackages/integrations/perplexity/\n├── src/\n│   ├── perplexity_client.py    # Core API client\n│   ├── perplexity_prism.py     # Lux prism wrapper\n│   ├── streaming_handler.py    # Streaming response support\n│   ├── model_selector.py       # Model selection logic\n│   └── cost_tracker.py         # Usage & cost tracking\n├── tests/\n│   ├── test_client.py          # Unit tests\n│   ├── test_streaming.py       # Streaming tests\n│   └── test_integration.py     # Integration tests\n├── examples/\n│   └── basic_usage.py          # Usage examples\n├── README.md\n└── requirements.txt\n```\n\n**Core Implementation**:\n```python\nclass PerplexityClient:\n    \"\"\"\n    Perplexity AI API client with streaming support\n    Supports models: sonar, sonar-pro, sonar-reasoning\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, api_key: str):\n        self.api_key = api_key\n        self.base_url = \"https://api.perplexity.ai\"\n        self.cost_tracker = CostTracker()\n    \n    async def chat_completion(\n        self,\n        messages: List[Dict],\n        model: str = \"sonar\",\n        stream: bool = False,\n        max_tokens: int = 1024\n    ) -> Union[Dict, AsyncIterator]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Send chat completion request\n        \n        Args:\n            messages: List of message dicts with role/content\n            model: Model name (sonar/sonar-pro/sonar-reasoning)\n            stream: Whether to stream response\n            max_tokens: Maximum tokens to generate\n        \n        Returns:\n            Complete response dict or async iterator for streaming\n        \"\"\"\n        headers = {\n            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {self.api_key}\",\n            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n        }\n        \n        payload = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": messages,\n            \"max_tokens\": max_tokens,\n            \"stream\": stream\n        }\n        \n        if stream:\n            return self._stream_response(headers, payload)\n        else:\n            return await self._complete_response(headers, payload)\n    \n    async def _stream_response(self, headers, payload):\n        \"\"\"Handle streaming response\"\"\"\n        async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session:\n            async with session.post(\n                f\"{self.base_url}/chat/completions\",\n                headers=headers,\n                json=payload\n            ) as response:\n                async for line in response.content:\n                    if line.startswith(b\"data: \"):\n                        data = json.loads(line[6:])\n                        yield self._parse_stream_chunk(data)\n                        \n                        # Track cost incrementally\n                        self.cost_tracker.add_token_usage(\n                            model=payload[\"model\"],\n                            input_tokens=data.get(\"usage\", {}).get(\"prompt_tokens\", 0),\n                            output_tokens=data.get(\"usage\", {}).get(\"completion_tokens\", 0)\n                        )\n    \n    def _parse_stream_chunk(self, data: Dict) -> Dict:\n        \"\"\"Parse streaming chunk into standard format\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"content\": data.get(\"choices\", [{}])[0].get(\"delta\", {}).get(\"content\", \"\"),\n            \"finish_reason\": data.get(\"choices\", [{}])[0].get(\"finish_reason\"),\n            \"usage\": data.get(\"usage\")\n        }\n```\n\n**Lux Prism Integration**:\n```python\nclass PerplexityPrism:\n    \"\"\"\n    Lux prism for Perplexity AI integration\n    Provides standardized interface for Lux beams\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, config: Dict):\n        self.client = PerplexityClient(config[\"api_key\"])\n        self.model_selector = ModelSelector()\n    \n    async def execute(self, input_data: Dict) -> Dict:\n        \"\"\"\n        Execute Perplexity query through Lux prism\n        \n        Input format:\n        {\n            \"query\": \"user question\",\n            \"context\": \"optional context\",\n            \"model\": \"sonar-pro\",  # optional\n            \"stream\": False        # optional\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n        # Select appropriate model\n        model = self.model_selector.select(\n            query=input_data.get(\"query\"),\n            preferred=input_data.get(\"model\")\n        )\n        \n        # Build messages\n        messages = self._build_messages(input_data)\n        \n        # Execute\n        response = await self.client.chat_completion(\n            messages=messages,\n            model=model,\n            stream=input_data.get(\"stream\", False)\n        )\n        \n        return {\n            \"answer\": response.get(\"choices\", [{}])[0].get(\"message\", {}).get(\"content\"),\n            \"citations\": response.get(\"citations\", []),\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"cost\": self.client.cost_tracker.get_last_call_cost()\n        }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Performance Estimation\n\n| Metric | Value | Notes |\n|--------|-------|-------|\n| API Latency | 500-2000ms | Depends on query complexity |\n| Streaming Latency | 50-100ms | First token arrival |\n| Token Throughput | ~50 tokens/sec | Streaming mode |\n| Memory Usage | ~10MB | Per client instance |\n| Concurrent Requests | 10+ | With connection pooling |\n\n**Cost Analysis** (Perplexity pricing):\n| Model | Input | Output | Example Cost (1K tokens) |\n|-------|-------|--------|-------------------------|\n| sonar | $0.20/M | $0.20/M | $0.0004 |\n| sonar-pro | $0.60/M | $0.60/M | $0.0012 |\n| sonar-reasoning | $1.00/M | $1.00/M | $0.0020 |\n\n**Optimization Strategies**:\n- Connection pooling for concurrent requests\n- Token usage tracking and budget alerts\n- Model selection based on query complexity\n- Response caching for common queries\n\n---\n\n### 3. Technical Q&A\n\n**Q1: How to handle Perplexity API rate limits?**\n\nA: Implement exponential backoff with jitter:\n```python\nasync def call_with_retry(self, func, max_retries=3):\n    for attempt in range(max_retries):\n        try:\n            return await func()\n        except RateLimitError as e:\n            wait_time = (2 ** attempt) + random.uniform(0, 1)\n            logger.warning(f\"Rate limited, waiting {wait_time}s\")\n            await asyncio.sleep(wait_time)\n    raise MaxRetriesExceeded()\n```\n\n**Q2: Streaming vs non-streaming - when to use each?**\n\nA:\n- **Streaming**: Real-time chat, long-form content, user-facing interfaces\n- **Non-streaming**: Background tasks, batch processing, simple Q&A\n\nImplementation supports both modes with unified interface.\n\n**Q3: How to integrate with existing Lux beam structure?**\n\nA: Follow Lux prism pattern:\n```python\n# Registration\nlux.register_prism(\"perplexity\", PerplexityPrism)\n\n# Usage in beam\nbeam = lux.create_beam()\nbeam.add_step(\"perplexity\", {\"query\": \"Explain quantum computing\"})\nresult = await beam.execute()\n```\n\n**Q4: Error handling strategy?**\n\nA: Multi-layer approach:\n1. **API Level**: Retry on 429, 500, 503\n2. **Client Level**: Circuit breaker for repeated failures\n3. **Application Level**: Graceful degradation to fallback models\n\n**Q5: Cost tracking implementation?**\n\nA: Real-time tracking with budget alerts:\n```python\nclass CostTracker:\n    def __init__(self, budget_limit: float = None):\n        self.total_cost = 0.0\n        self.budget_limit = budget_limit\n        self.calls = []\n    \n    def add_token_usage(self, model: str, input_tokens: int, output_tokens: int):\n        cost = self._calculate_cost(model, input_tokens, output_tokens)\n        self.total_cost += cost\n        \n        if self.budget_limit and self.total_cost > self.budget_limit:\n            logger.warning(f\"Budget exceeded: ${self.total_cost:.4f}\")\n            raise BudgetExceededError()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Timeline\n\n| Phase | Duration | Deliverables |\n|-------|----------|--------------|\n| API Client | 2h | PerplexityClient with auth, error handling |\n| Streaming | 2h | Streaming response handler |\n| Prism Integration | 2h | Lux prism wrapper, model selector |\n| Cost Tracking | 1h | CostTracker with budget alerts |\n| Testing | 2h | Unit tests (>80% coverage), integration tests |\n| Documentation | 1h | README, usage examples |\n| **Total** | **10h** | **~1-1.5 days** |\n\n**Buffer**: +2h for review feedback\n\n---\n\n### 5. Experience\n\n**Related Projects**:\n- **LLM Integrations**: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini clients\n- **Streaming APIs**: Built real-time streaming handlers for multiple providers\n- **Lux Framework**: Familiar with prism/beam architecture (see Lux contributions)\n\n**Technical Background**:\n- 5+ years Python/asyncio development\n- 3+ years LLM/AI integrations\n- Experience with API rate limiting, error handling\n- Built cost tracking systems for AI services\n\n---\n\n### Ready to Start\n\nI have a clear understanding of the requirements and can begin implementation immediately upon approval.\n\n**Approach**: Start with core client, add streaming, then integrate with Lux prism structure.\n\nLooking forward to your feedback!\n\ncc: @maintainers\n","createdAt":"2026-02-28T03:06:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-3976210907","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCXoO_w","author":{"login":"zp6"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #97\nWorking on this issue. Will submit a PR shortly.","createdAt":"2026-05-14T19:16:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-4453961471","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCX4Xkw","author":{"login":"zp6"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi! I've implemented the Perplexity AI integration for this issue. PR #595 is ready for review.\n\n**Summary:**\n- Lux.Integrations.Perplexity - Client module with chat completion, cost estimation, model listing\n- Lux.Prisms.Perplexity.Search - Web search with citations and domain filtering\n- Lux.Prisms.Perplexity.Ask - Knowledge-intensive Q&A with context injection\n- Lux.Prisms.Perplexity.ModelInfo - Model selection with filtering\n- Comprehensive unit tests for all modules\n\nThe PR builds on the existing Lux.LLM.Perplexity module already in main, adding the integration layer and prisms on top.","createdAt":"2026-05-14T19:54:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-4454225811","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABD-rw2Q","author":{"login":"JirA44"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Taking this — Perplexity API client following the same Lux.LLM pattern as OpenAI/Anthropic. PR coming.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T08:15:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-4562022617","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABD_bdnA","author":{"login":"faisalnugroho"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I would like to work on this bounty.\n\n**Approach:**\n- Implement Perplexity API client with search-augmented generation\n- Support for online and offline models\n- Citation tracking and source verification\n- Cost optimization with model selection\n- Integration with Lux's LLM abstraction layer\n\n**Timeline:** 3-5 days\n\nReady to start immediately.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T09:52:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-4562804124","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABISwSNw","author":{"login":"bambooshadow-studio"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #97\n\nSubmitted PR #897: https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/pull/897\n\nImplements Perplexity AI LLM provider with:\n- OpenAI-compatible chat completions API\n- Search-grounded responses with citation support\n- Configurable model selection (sonar-pro, sonar)\n- Standard Lux.LLM behaviour compliance","createdAt":"2026-07-01T07:31:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97#issuecomment-4851503671","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2025-02-25T11:06:23Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB2iNfMA","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"},{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6PoGQw","name":"bounty","description":"","color":"395808"},{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6P9AOQ","name":"llm","description":"Issues related to LLM integrations and features","color":"0366d6"},{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6ZjxQg","name":"in-progress","description":"","color":"f9d0c4"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"Perplexity AI Integration $300","updatedAt":"2026-07-01T07:31:20Z","url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/97"}
